{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpretation of the completed receipt e19ad6d076fa4d878b7bd0f90f067fca (completed, exit_code 0) for investigation b2266ae85cad4e4db077a5615b2b892c-question-0. Parsed events: indices 8, 9, 10 and 11 are the absent_server case (admission, 1500 ms window, bounded client write, recovery after the named server is started) and indices 12, 13, 14 and 15 are the control with the named server running beforehand; indices 0-7 and 16-20 belong to the two earlier harness scenarios that share the file. The receipt contradicts part of the hypothesis recorded with the question and confirms the rest, so this interpretation corrects the account rather than restating it: the configuration entry does commit, but leadership and the ability to elect are lost immediately afterwards. A fact is added for the corrected account.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"b2266ae85cad4e4db077a5615b2b892c-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"01878d6cc9e24ccb8fd3d9157f560ea3-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"addvoter-doc-staging-promise\\\",\\\"bootstrapcluster-growth-guidance\\\",\\\"appendconfiguration-installs-latest\\\",\\\"commitment-recalculate-quorum\\\",\\\"commitment-set-configuration\\\",\\\"checkleaderlease-latest-quorum\\\",\\\"quorumsize-latest\\\",\\\"requestconfigchange-timeout-scope\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"e19ad6d076fa4d878b7bd0f90f067fca\\\":[8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Admission (index 8): a real single-voter cluster, leader at term 2 with commit index 2 and last index 2, its configuration listing only itself, and the named second server's identity derived from a transport that is not wired to the cluster and has no raft running (named_server_up false); the configuration entry will be index 3. Window (index 9): the commit index moves from 2 to 3 within the first samples, so the configuration entry does commit, and the AddVoter future completes with no error (future_resolved true, future_error null). This contradicts the prediction recorded with the question that the configuration entry could not commit: dispatchLogs calls commitment.match for the leader before appendConfigurationEntry installs the new configuration, so the entry is matched under the previous single-voter quorum and committed, and only afterwards does the new configuration govern. What follows is nonetheless the predicted consequence: the sampled state is Leader for the first three samples, then Follower, then Candidate for the remaining samples; the node stays a Candidate at term 2 for the whole window (term_samples contains only 2), because pre-vote does not advance the term, and it cannot win anyway since the new configuration's quorum is two and only one server answers. Client work (index 10) is refused with 'node is not the leader' and the commit index stays 3: the cluster, which in this configuration is the only node, has no leader and no further progress. Recovery (index 11): as soon as the named server is started at its announced address and wired in, the original node wins at term 3 and becomes Leader again with the named node following, so the state is repairable by the event the caller controls. Control (indices 12-15): with the named server running before the call, the leader stays Leader in all 59 samples, the commit index reaches 3, a client write succeeds (write_error null, commit 4) and the growth completes normally. The two cases differ only in whether the named server was already running, so the absent server is the cause. Corrected account: following the sequence BootstrapCluster's documentation recommends (bootstrap one voter, then AddVoter the next server) makes the cluster unavailable when the next server has not been started yet, and the API reports success because the configuration change itself commits. The harm is availability, not safety: no committed entry is lost, and the single node never splits into two leaders. Predicate evaluated: following the documented growth sequence with the next server not yet running must not remove the ability to serve, or must at least be reported as a failure by the API that performed it. It is contradicted by the witness: the AddVoter future reports success while the only node loses leadership, cannot be re-elected under the configuration it just committed, and refuses client writes with ErrNotLeader. Scope: configuration version 3, a single-voter configuration grown by one voter, the new configuration's quorum (2 of 2) therefore requiring the new server, no faults, one process, in-memory transport.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The recorded prediction that the configuration entry cannot commit is refuted by this receipt: commit_index reaches the configuration entry's index before the leader steps down, because the leader's own match is recorded against the previous configuration's quorum. The defect account is corrected accordingly; the unavailability comes from the lease quorum and from the election quorum of the committed configuration, not from an uncommitted entry.\\\",\n   \\\"Recovery is automatic and caller-controlled: starting the named server restores leadership within the same execution (index 11), so the harm window ends when the operator performs the step the sequence implies.\\\",\n   \\\"The safe alternatives exist inside the library: AddNonvoter first (non-voters receive log entries without counting for quorum) and AddVoter only when the server is up, or start the server before AddVoter as the control does. The defect is therefore about the documented sequence and the successful API result, not about a missing capability.\\\",\n   \\\"The named server's absence is the caller's input; the audit-relevant part is that the library's own documentation recommends this ordering and still describes AddVoter as adding a staging server that is promoted once ready.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"One retained execution, one process, in-memory transport, one configuration shape (1 to 2 voters) and short timeouts; in the observed run the loss of leadership happened about 75 ms after the call (three samples) and the window measured 1500 ms, so the production duration scales with LeaderLeaseTimeout and then lasts as long as the named server is absent.\\\",\n   \\\"Only the 1-to-2 growth step is exercised here; the same step from two or more voters keeps a quorum among the survivors, so the finding is scoped to that step and to any configuration whose new quorum cannot be met without the absent server.\\\",\n   \\\"The control is a separate single-voter cluster built later in the same execution rather than the same cluster with the server present, so the comparison is between equivalent configurations rather than the same cluster instance.\\\",\n   \\\"The documentation statements are treated as normative source text, not as an enforced contract; the code has no check that the named server is reachable, and the deprecation of the Staging suffrage left the AddVoter documentation describing behaviour that the code no longer implements.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"按库自身文档的顺序扩展单节点集群会让集群失去领导者：AddVoter 报告成功却拒绝写入\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"已确认的有源缺陷（A1 进度 / A2 成员与权限）：BootstrapCluster 的文档建议先以单个 Voter 引导、再用 AddVoter 加入其他服务器，而 AddVoter 的文档仍沿用旧的 staging 语义（加入后『待其就绪再提升为 Voter』）。本快照中 AddVoter 会立即把目标写入最新配置并作为 Voter 生效。保留执行 e19ad6d076fa4d878b7bd0f90f067fca 显示：在真实单节点集群上对一台尚未启动的服务器调用 AddVoter 后，该配置项在旧配置的法定人数下立即提交（commit 2→3），AddVoter future 返回 nil（成功）；但随后唯一的节点被降为 Follower、再变为 Candidate ——状态采样为 Leader×3 → Follower → Candidate，整个 1500 毫秒窗口内 term 恒为 2（预投票避免了任期膨胀），之后客户端写入被拒（node is not the leader），commit 停在上限。也就是说：整个（单节点）集群在命名服务器出现之前不可用，而触发它的 API 却报告成功；一旦该服务器在其地址上启动，集群自动恢复（原节点在 term 3 重新当选）。对照实验（同一调用，但服务器已先启动）则全程保持 Leader、写入成功。该缺陷是可用性问题而非安全性问题（无已提交条目丢失、无双 Leader），但文档所推荐的扩展顺序与实际行为相矛盾，且 safe 路径（先 AddNonvoter、就绪后再 AddVoter 提升）在库中存在却未被文档指引。\\\"\n }],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\n  \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@absent-voter-deposes-sole-node\\\",\n  \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"On a single-voter cluster, AddVoter for a server that is not running yet commits the configuration change (the leader's own match is recorded against the previous configuration's quorum) and the future completes successfully, after which the only node loses leadership within the lease timeout and remains a Candidate that cannot be re-elected under the configuration it just committed, so client writes are refused with ErrNotLeader until the named server appears; pre-vote keeps its term unchanged throughout, and starting the named server restores leadership.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Protocol version 3, a configuration with exactly one voter grown by one voter (so the new configuration's quorum cannot be met by the surviving server), the named server not running, no faults, in-memory transport. Observed with 25 ms sampling for 1500 ms after the call, with the same call on an equivalent cluster whose named server was already running as the control.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"addvoter-doc-staging-promise\\\",\\\"bootstrapcluster-growth-guidance\\\",\\\"appendconfiguration-installs-latest\\\",\\\"commitment-recalculate-quorum\\\",\\\"checkleaderlease-latest-quorum\\\",\\\"quorumsize-latest\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"e19ad6d076fa4d878b7bd0f90f067fca\\\":[8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15]}\n }]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\nprint('ok', d['interpretations'][0]['conclusion'], d['interpretations'][0]['defect_claim'], d['interpretations'][0]['executions'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
